      "usage": {
        "input_tokens": 39428,
        "output_tokens": 394,
        "calls": 2,
        "seconds": 6.81
      },
      "text": "A player is in an offside position if, when a teammate plays or touches the ball, they are in the opponents' half and ahead of both the ball and the second-last defender (hands/arms don't count; level is onside). Position alone isn't an offence — they must then interfere with play, interfere with an opponent, or gain an advantage from a rebound, deflection or save. Direct receipt from a throw-in, corner or goal kick is exempt. A deliberate opponent play usually resets the situation; a deliberate save does not. An offside offence results in an indirect free kick.",
